const introParagraphs = [
  "<strong>Del Mar runs on a calendar no other city on our routes has: quiet streets most of the year, then the racetrack and fairgrounds season fills every second home at once — and every appliance that spent months switched off gets asked to perform for a full house on day one. Our San Diego technicians work both halves of that cycle: pre-season checkouts before the houses fill, and fast response when a machine that 'was fine last summer' turns out not to be. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</strong>",
  "Here's the counterintuitive physics of a Del Mar kitchen: the ocean is hardest on the appliances that aren't running. A refrigerator in daily use moves air across its condenser and sheds the salt film as it goes; a second-home unit powered down in October sits in marine air for eight months while the film builds undisturbed, gaskets dry into their folds, and drain traps evaporate open. Then July arrives, the house fills, and the machine is asked to sprint from a standing start. Most of the 'sudden' failures we see in 92014 were eight months in the making — in an empty house where nobody could hear them coming.",
  "The town splits at the 101. West of it, the beach colony: cottages and contemporary rebuilds on the sand where everything mechanical lives closest to the water — and where many houses stand empty between race weeks and holidays. East of it, the hillside — Del Mar Heights and the canyon-edge streets — with year-round households, bigger kitchens, and the same imported hard water that scales dishwashers and ice makers all along the corridor. Two different service rhythms, five minutes apart.",
  "For owners who are elsewhere most of the year, we work the way second homes require: keyholder and house-sitter coordination, written estimates approved by phone or email from another time zone, photos of what we found, and a pre-arrival checkout that runs every machine before the family lands — because discovering the ice maker is dead on the first morning of race week is a Del Mar tradition nobody actually wants.",
  `Diagnostic fee: <strong>$89</strong> — waived with repair. Written estimate before we start. <strong>90-day warranty</strong> on parts and labor. Call <a href="tel:${phoneRaw}">${branch.phone}</a> for service across 92014 — and the rest of the <a href="/san-diego-county/">North Coastal corridor</a>.`
];

