    "Every coastal page we publish talks about salt air, so here is the Del Mar-specific version: running machines defend themselves, idle machines don't. Airflow, heat cycles, and vibration keep a working refrigerator shedding moisture and film; a unit powered down for the off-season just sits there while marine air settles into it. Door gaskets dry in the folded position and split on first opening. Trap water evaporates and lets odors migrate. Fill valves crust closed. The first week of occupancy then exposes eight months of quiet accumulation all at once.",
